bug_report.RootCause:
1) StaticFilesHandlerMixin missing async response method (django/contrib/staticfiles/handlers.py: class StaticFilesHandlerMixin). The ASGI path calls get_response_async but the mixin only implements get_response (sync). The correct relationship is that the mixin must provide get_response_async that mirrors get_response but runs the synchronous serve() and response_for_exception through sync_to_async. Concretely: async def get_response_async(self, request):
    try:
        return await sync_to_async(self.serve, thread_sensitive=True)(request)
    except Http404 as e:
        return await sync_to_async(response_for_exception, thread_sensitive=True)(request, e)

2) ASGIHandler.__call__ (django/core/handlers/asgi.py) invokes await self.get_response_async(request). Because StaticFilesHandlerMixin lacks get_response_async, Python falls back to BaseHandler.get_response_async (django/core/handlers/base.py), which calls await self._middleware_chain(request). That relationship (get_response_async -> await self._middleware_chain(request)) assumes load_middleware has populated self._middleware_chain.

3) StaticFilesHandlerMixin overrides load_middleware as a no-op (django/contrib/staticfiles/handlers.py: StaticFilesHandlerMixin.load_middleware), so wrapper instances do not populate _middleware_chain. Combined with (1), this leads to BaseHandler.get_response_async attempting to call self._middleware_chain which is None, producing TypeError. 

4) ASGIStaticFilesHandler.__init__ (django/contrib/staticfiles/handlers.py: class ASGIStaticFilesHandler.__init__) does not call super().__init__(), so ASGIHandler.__init__ (which would call load_middleware(is_async=True) in normal initialization) is never invoked on the instance. Even though the mixin's load_middleware is intentionally a no-op, the missing initialization makes the ASGI wrapper's initialization diverge from the WSGI counterpart and contributes to the observed failure when get_response_async is absent.

